[thin] These picks terminate at the Z 7.06 junction of the open inspection window and the horizontal end retention caps. The submillimetre closest approaches are along that sharp boundary; exact STEP occupancy at the representative picks has stock on one side of Z 7.06 and air on the other. They do not define a submillimetre nominal roof. The end caps have 3.00 mm vertical roof stock and preserve the flat body clearance.
alternatives: Larger rounded window ends remove the sharp junction but shorten or move the flat retaining region and need an updated engagement comparison. Closing the inspection window leaves larger continuous stock but hides the tongue and limits support-removal access. A thicker outward cap preserves the fit but increases overall height without changing this terminating boundary.
